        {
          "event": "Coastal Flood Advisory",
          "headline": "Coastal Flood Advisory issued October 7 at 12:33PM PDT until October 13 at 3:00PM PDT by NWS San Francisco CA",
          "severity": "Minor",
          "urgency": "Expected",
          "description": "* WHAT...Up to 1.2 ft of inundation above ground level is\npossible in low-lying areas near shorelines and tidal waterways.\n\n* WHERE...Bayshore locations along the San Francisco and Monterey\nBays.\n\n* WHEN...From 9 AM Friday to 3 PM PDT Tuesday.\n\n* IMPACTS...Flooding of lots, parks, and roads with only\nisolated road closures expected. High tides will result in\nflooding along coastal trails, cut off access to some low-\nlying beaches and coastal areas, and bring water and waves\nfarther up the beach than typical.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...At the San Francisco tidal gauge, high tide\nis expected to be 1.0 ft above normal (6.86 ft MLLW) at 11:22\nAM Friday 10/9, 1.2 ft above normal (7.06 ft MLLW) at 11:50 AM\nSaturday 10/10, 1.2 ft above normal (7.08 ft MLLW) at 12:18 PM\nSunday 10/11, 1.2 ft above normal (7.03 ft MLLW) at 12:46 PM\nMonday 10/12, 1.1 ft above normal (6.90 ft MLLW) at 1:14 PM\nTuesday 10/13, and 0.9 ft above normal (6.72 ft MLLW) at 1:46 PM\nWednesday 10/14. These predictions include up to 1.0 ft of\nsurge that will enhance the astronomical tide and flooding\nthreat. High tide varies up to 90 minutes earlier or later along\nthe Pacific Coast and through the San Francisco Bay,\nrespectively.",
          "instruction": "If travel is required, allow extra time as some roads may be\nclosed. Do not drive around barricades or through water of\nunknown depth. Take the necessary actions to protect flood-prone\nproperty.",
          "expires": "2026-10-08T13:00:00-07:00",
          "source_url": "https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.3ae2ebe2f5bd5a06768ab277e7d14bff22d75e9f.001.1"
        }
      ]
